\title{Several plans started at once, each trading its own quantity}
\description{
The \code{together} join of a plan: one to twenty-five plans started at once, each trading its own quantity.

Unlike an \code{either} join, a fill on one child does nothing to the others, so a together join is how a plan sends a basket, a pair or a spread whose legs are independent. By default UBI's broker selector chooses a broker that can afford the whole group, and \code{hedge_benefit} prices hedged legs as one position. With \code{done_when} set to \code{any}, the rest are cancelled once one child is done. A together join cannot be a \code{then} join's child, because that child is sized to the first plan's fills.
}
